This blocked the ENTIRE solution build for every prompt, not just this one.

Remediation is documented in the file's own header invariant: "regenerate it
directly from the Microsoft.UI-free sources on disk ... exactly ONE Project root
... ONE Compile ItemGroup (case-insensitive ordinal path-sorted, Include-dedup
union of every Microsoft.UI-free .cs under dashboard-widgets/ feature-views/
misc-surfaces/ modals-dialogs/ shared-surfaces/)".

Action taken (deterministic regeneration):
  - Authored a clean single-root header from scratch (the on-disk header prose
    was itself corrupted) — PropertyGroup + package/project-ref/content ItemGroups
    verbatim, plus a well-formed invariant comment (no "--" inside the XML comment).
  - Re-derived the Compile ItemGroup from disk. A source is "Microsoft.UI-free"
    when it has no `using Microsoft.UI` / `using Windows.UI` directive (doc-comment
    mentions of "Microsoft.UI-free" do NOT count). This reproduced the pre-corruption
    set EXACTLY: 1299 entries, 0 added, 0 dropped, identical order/format (verified
    by diff against the surviving block-1 Compile group).
  - Extended the union with the new 6th category widget-primitives/ (Link prefix
    WidgetPrimitives\) for this surface's two Microsoft.UI-free sources.
  - Normalised to LF + final newline per apps/.editorconfig (end_of_line = lf).
  Result: 1 <Project> root, 1301 <Compile> entries, valid XML, LF.

