================================================================================
PARITY MAP (web -> native)
================================================================================
RadialGauge (size 70/100)        -> TsRadialGauge (Components/Charts), Diameter 70/100
gauge.color (hex "#3b82f6")      -> ChartRole / ColorIndex token selectors (ADR-009:
                                    no ported hex; tints from W1 palette, theme-aware)
flex-col items-center gap-2      -> vertical StackPanel, centred, Spacing 8
stats flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-1  -> centred horizontal StackPanel, Spacing 16
stat label  text-xs secondary    -> TextBlock 12 / TsColorTextSecondaryBrush, ellipsis
stat value  text-sm semibold     -> Run 14 SemiBold / TsColorTextPrimaryBrush
stat unit   ml-0.5 xs normal      -> inline Run 12 Normal / TsColorTextSecondaryBrush
children (!compact)              -> Footer (object?) via ContentPresenter, !compact gated
value clamp + fmt (RadialGauge)  -> clamp 0..max; int -> 0 dp, else global precision 2

================================================================================
STATES REPRODUCED (every branch of the web source renders; never blank)
================================================================================
[x] standard + stats          -> gauge + centred stats row
[x] standard + no/empty stats -> gauge alone (the "empty stats" branch), never blank
[x] standard + children       -> gauge (+ stats) + footer content
[x] compact                   -> 70px gauge only; stats + children suppressed
[x] zero/!finite value        -> gauge still renders a named "0" (never a blank box)
Note: loading/error/stale/offline are owned by the consuming widget (e.g.
DriveScoreGaugeWidget), not this presentational primitive — matching the web source,
whose Data sources = none. Reproducing them here would be invented scope (drift).

